## External packages installed at converge

VSCodium is a separate MIT-licensed work. The `developer` role adds VSCodium's
official APT repository and installs the `codium` package only when the
`vscodium` group is selected in `developer_tools`; the product neither
redistributes nor relicenses it. The repository key is pinned by checksum and
fingerprint in `roles/developer/defaults/main.yml`.

The Scripts interpreter is a separate work under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or later (`GPL-3.0-or-later`), published by the same author at
<https://github.com/benmoussa-younes/scripts>. The `developer` role installs its
latest Debian release package only when the `scripts` group is selected, after
verifying the release's `SHA256SUMS`. The product neither redistributes nor
relicenses it.

Mozilla Firefox is a separate work under the Mozilla Public License 2.0. The
`applications` role adds Mozilla's official APT repository and installs the
`firefox` package; the product neither redistributes nor relicenses it. The
repository key is pinned by checksum and fingerprint in
`roles/applications/defaults/main.yml`.

OpenCode is a separate work under its own upstream licence. The
`coding_agents` role downloads its vendor installer only when the role is
enabled, verifies the installer against a declared SHA-256, and installs the
pinned version for the human account; the product neither redistributes nor
relicenses the binary, and it declares no model, provider or credential.

Steam is proprietary software. The opt-in `gaming` role installs Debian's
`steam-installer` package from `contrib` and the 32-bit graphics stack it
needs; the product neither redistributes nor relicenses Steam itself, and the
role is inert unless `gaming_enabled` is true.

The .NET SDK is a separate MIT-licensed work. The `developer` role adds
Microsoft's official Debian repository and installs `dotnet-sdk-10.0` only
when `developer_tools` selects the `dotnet` group; the product neither
redistributes nor relicenses it. The key is pinned by checksum and fingerprint
in `roles/developer/defaults/main.yml`.

## Ansible and Debian

Ansible is a separate work, installed by the controller. Debian is a separate
distribution, installed on the target; `gnome-core` and every other package come
from it. Neither is redistributed by this collection. The product uses only
`ansible.builtin`; `requirements.yml` declares no external collection.
